# WN22-CC-000190: Windows Server 2022 users must be prompted to authenticate when the system wakes from sleep (plugged in).
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-cc-000190-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 users must be prompted to authenticate when the system wakes from sleep (plugged in).`
    description `A system that does not require authentication when resuming from sleep may provide access to unauthorized users. Authentication must always be required when accessing a system. This setting ensures users are prompted for a password when the system wakes from sleep (plugged in).`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> System >> Power Management >> Sleep Settings >> Require a password when a computer wakes (plugged in) to "Enabled".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by setting registry value 'ACSettingIndex' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by setting registry value 'ACSettingIndex' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by setting registry value 'ACSettingIndex' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by setting registry value 'ACSettingIndex' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by setting registry value 'ACSettingIndex' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Power\PowerSettings\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51`
        name `ACSettingIndex`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 1
